  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: scVI n200 (config_004, acc 0.520) is our best result and clearly outperforms PCA n2000 (config_001, acc 0.485), establishing a strong RNA encoder. Image-only (config_010, acc 0.208) is very weak, making the RNA pathway the dominant signal. Uncertainty: We have zero data on whether multiprofile aggregation can improve upon single-profile performance, and this is a fundamental design axis that will affect all downstream multimodal experiments. Question: Does aggregating multiple profiles with a transformer (the most expressive aggregation) on top of the best RNA encoder (scVI n200) yield a meaningful gain over the single-profile baseline? Why this is the best next experiment: It directly extends our strongest result along the most unexplored and consequential dimension (profile count + aggregation), uses the most powerful aggregation to establish an upper bound, and the answer will inform whether subsequent multimodal experiments should use single or multiprofile. If transformer aggregation fails to improve, avgpool likely won't either, saving future budget."
}

